# Third-party licences

**Generated — do not edit by hand.** Regenerate with:

```
cargo about generate about.hbs -o LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY.md
```

Aloud is distributed as a single statically-linked binary. Everything below is
compiled into it, so its licence obligations travel with every copy of Aloud.
This file discharges the attribution obligation common to all of them.

**Two things are NOT in this file**, because they are not Rust dependencies:

- **The Supertonic TTS model weights** — BigScience OpenRAIL-M, a *use-restricted*
  licence, not merely an attribution one. Full text in `supertonic-weights-OpenRAIL-M.txt`.
  The weights are downloaded at runtime and are not part of this binary.
  See `LICENSES/README.md` for why the code and the weights must never be conflated.
- **ONNX Runtime** — MIT (Microsoft), linked as a prebuilt static library fetched by
  `ort-sys` at build time rather than as a crates.io dependency, so `cargo-about`
  cannot see it. Its licence text is at
  <https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/blob/main/LICENSE>.

**On MPL-2.0.** Some components below are Mozilla Public License 2.0, which is
file-level copyleft rather than attribution-only. Distributing them inside Aloud is
expressly permitted (MPL-2.0 §3.3, "Larger Works"), but recipients must be able to
obtain the source of those files. Aloud uses every one of them **unmodified**, so the
upstream links below satisfy that. If one is ever vendored and edited, the
modifications must themselves be published under MPL-2.0.

